.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN.\n\n**Change:** `round_money` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. For example, `2.665` now rounds to `2.66` instead of `2.68`.\n\n**CI:** passed on 08d3cd5986 (run ci-0001).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and the pull request is open with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed: with the old setting, `2.665` rounded to `2.68` instead of `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, `round_money` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** [#101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101) against `main`.\n\nI didn't merge it, because merging into `main` needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}